
Fashion MNIST Classification Using Neural Network

About the Project

This project uses a simple Neural Network to classify images of clothing items from the Fashion MNIST dataset. The project also studies how learning rate and number of epochs affect model accuracy.

Dataset

Fashion MNIST is a built-in dataset provided by TensorFlow. It contains 70,000 grayscale images of clothing items.

There are 10 classes, such as T-shirt, Trouser, Pullover, Dress, Coat, Sandal, Shirt, Sneaker, Bag, and Ankle Boot.

The images are 28 × 28 pixels and are converted into 784 values before training.

What We Do

1. Load the Fashion MNIST dataset using TensorFlow.
2. Normalize the pixel values and reshape the images.
3. Build a neural network with two hidden layers.
4. Test different learning rates: 0.1, 0.01, and 0.001.
5. Test different numbers of epochs: 5, 10, and 20.
6. Train the final model using a learning rate of 0.001 for 20 epochs.
7. Compare training and validation accuracy and loss.
8. Evaluate the model using test accuracy.
9. Display predicted clothing classes and a confusion matrix.
